module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterE.Section04.GenerationBound.LocalControl.QuasisimpleFactor.OuterSylow

/-!
# The quasisimple local quotient branch of E.4.2

The local core fixed space has a pointwise kernel whose image contains the
quasisimple generalized Fitting subgroup of H/O₂(H). If that factor times
the Sylow image is normal, the kernel-times-Sylow criterion proves eventual
invariance. This includes all two-group quotients above the local factor.

The remaining case, where the factor times the Sylow image is not normal,
is not resolved here. The full source branch must still use the genuine
global representation and generating-family hypotheses to handle it. These
reductions do not assert an unconditional E.4.2 theorem or the blanket
residual commutator identity from its printed proof.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, E.4.2,
printed p.241 (PDF p.252).
-/
